      "repository": "gordolio/Trio",
      "number": 26,
      "title": "feat(isftest): Add the guided ISF test and run settings tests in a service",
      "body": "Adds the guided ISF test (#21) and moves both settings tests into `SettingsTestService`, so a test settles, cancels on a spoiled bolus, ends on a low and finishes with its screen closed. A notification says when a step needs you or the test ends, and tapping it opens that screen, even when it starts Trio. Upstream changes are one line each in `AppDelegate` and `UserNotificationsManager`.\n\n![ISF Dose Ready notification](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/623d6ede-dbe7-4515-a5bc-5b6cc0e6adb3) ![Dose step opened from the notification](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/965e8025-76ea-4f3a-a542-77c905a8d763)\n\nTested with the unit suites and on the iOS 27.2 simulator (17 Pro, SE): a spoiled bolus from Home, endings in the background, and notification taps from a cold launch. Draft while an adversarial review runs and before the device matrix.\n\n#21 · [ISF testing method](https://triodocs.org/usage/concepts/isf/#testing-method)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added ISF Testing alongside Basal Testing, with guided steps for checking readiness, raising glucose when needed, calculating a dose, monitoring progress, and reviewing results.\n  * Added ISF test schedules and history to the settings hub, with guidance when settings may affect a test.\n  * Added clearer test status, glucose and insulin information, progress charts, and notifications for relevant test updates.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved test handling around stale or missing readings, changing pump conditions, and tests that end early.\n  * Prevented older data refreshes from replacing newer displayed information and disabled stop actions while a test is ending.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
      "labels": [],
